::ENG1_U05_L01_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Sentence: The report explain how tutoring helps students revise essays. Which revision uses standard English?
{
=A. The report explains how tutoring helps students revise essays. #Correct. The singular subject report needs the singular verb explains, and the meaning stays the same.
~B. The report explaining how tutoring helps students revise essays. #Incorrect. This creates an incomplete sentence because the main verb is missing.
~C. The report explain how tutoring helps students revises essays. #Incorrect. Both verb forms create agreement problems and make the sentence less clear.
~D. The reports explains how tutoring helps students revise essays. #Incorrect. The plural subject reports does not match the singular verb explains.
}

::ENG1_U05_L01_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Draft: Students used the media center it was quiet before school. Which revision fixes the sentence boundary?
{
~A. Students used the media center it quiet before school. #Incorrect. This removes a verb and still does not create a clear sentence boundary.
=B. Students used the media center because it was quiet before school. #Correct. The word because connects the two ideas clearly and fixes the run-on sentence.
~C. Students used the media center quiet before school. #Incorrect. This sentence leaves out the relationship between the media center and quiet conditions.
~D. Students used the media center, it was quiet before school. #Incorrect. A comma alone cannot correctly join two complete sentences.
}

::ENG1_U05_L01_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Sentence: The survey and article were useful because it explained student concerns. Which revision improves pronoun clarity?
{
~A. The survey and article were useful because it was useful. #Incorrect. The pronoun it remains unclear and repeats the same vague idea.
=B. The survey and article were useful because both sources explained student concerns. #Correct. Both sources clearly names what the pronoun should refer to.
~C. The survey and article were useful because they was clear. #Incorrect. The pronoun they is clearer, but the verb was does not agree.
~D. The survey and article were useful because student concerns explained it. #Incorrect. This changes the meaning and creates a confusing sentence.
}

::ENG1_U05_L01_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG1.W.04] Draft: Online calendars helps students track due dates. Which explanation best describes the needed correction?
{
~A. The sentence needs a comma after Online. #Incorrect. The main issue is not punctuation; the subject and verb do not agree.
~B. The word calendars should be capitalized. #Incorrect. Calendars is not a proper noun here, so capitalization is not the problem.
=C. The plural subject calendars needs the verb help. #Correct. The correction is Online calendars help students track due dates, which fixes agreement.
~D. The sentence should remove students. #Incorrect. Removing students would damage the meaning instead of fixing the convention problem.
}

::ENG1_U05_L01_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Draft: The reminders is useful because they shows missing work. Which revision is best?
{
~A. The reminders is useful because it shows missing work. #Incorrect. It improves pronoun number but still leaves the plural subject reminders with is.
~B. The reminder are useful because they show missing work. #Incorrect. Reminder is singular, so it does not match are or they.
~C. The reminders useful because they show missing work. #Incorrect. This removes the needed verb and creates a fragment.
=D. The reminders are useful because they show missing work. #Correct. The plural subject reminders matches are and the plural pronoun they matches reminders.
}
